==Battleground==
*The enemy base here is a [[Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Doge Base]].
*3 [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*8 [[Gardeneel Bros.]] spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 36.67~43.33 seconds<sup>1,100f~1,300f</sup>.
*1 [[Oldhorn]] spawns as the boss after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Celeboodle]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Sir Rel]]s spawn after 80 seconds<sup>2,400f</sup>, delay 13.33~20 seconds<sup>400f~600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage aims to get Gardeneel to warp your units to trigger Doge Base, which then wipes out your stack. However, this does not work because you can just get something like [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Octopus Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]] warped and then beat up the base. If this doesn't happen, just use strong anti-Relics and Wave Immune units like [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] to win. If you have [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]], its level 7 Wave is actually able to hit Gardeneel while using Oldhorn as a stepping stone, which makes this level a lot more simple.

==Trivia==
*Like all [[Unearthed Artifacts]] stages, Loser's Complaint's Japanese name references an idiom. In this case, the name Maken no Tōboe (魔犬の遠吠え, "Demon Dog's Howl") is a play on the idiom ''makeinu no tōboe'', (負け犬の遠吠え, "Loser Dog's Howl"), which refers to when a loser in a fight refuses to admit defeat behind their opponent's back.

